--- src.orig/chrome/browser/ui/cocoa/arcium_settings_swift/VENDOR_PROVENANCE.md
+++ src/chrome/browser/ui/cocoa/arcium_settings_swift/VENDOR_PROVENANCE.md
@@ -28,3 +28,16 @@ Arcium form hierarchy keeps flat setting
 Grouped section headings use the section type style and header accessibility
 traits; glow-editor subheadings use a smaller secondary style distinct from card
 titles. The host retains the package's existing aligned row controls.
+
+Space theme controls share one accent-and-palette row. Chrome and website modes
+use matching segmented controls. Section headings use 18pt type, a restrained
+resolved-accent tint and a fading rule, with stronger neutral styling for
+Increased Contrast. Empty headings do not gain decorative rules.
+
+Local appearance extension: reversible None / Tint / Glows policy preserves saved color recipes, supports empty glow palettes, and disables inactive decorative controls.
+
+The Address bar group exposes centering, minimal display and the existing top-bar
+pin together. The pin applies to Fully hidden sidebars and Zen mode; it retains
+the existing host preference, saved values and managed-availability checks.
+
+Tint has a direct color well independent of saved glow points. Its optional Space-owned seed uses the native shared palette for contrast and the flat preview.
